# The paths specy-road writes at run time are ignored by the managed block
# below, which `specy-road init project` writes and `specy-road refresh-stubs`
# keeps current. Add your own rules outside the block; the block is rewritten.
# The comments here explain what the block ignores, and what it deliberately
# leaves tracked.
#
# work/ runtime artifacts are ignored by default (`work/*`): briefs,
# implementation summaries, prompts, PR-body snapshots, brainstorm sessions,
# chore records, review hand-offs (work/reviews/), session presence
# (work/.sessions/), worker records and linked worktrees (work/.workers/,
# work/.worktrees/) and the work/done/ archive. A review binds to the commit
# it read, so committing it would move the branch past that commit; the other
# files are regenerated or local to one checkout. Implementation summaries are
# therefore local (roadmap/git-workflow.yaml `implementation_summary: local`):
# a reviewer in another clone does not see the summary.
#
# work/README.md, work/.gitkeep and the top-level work/*.template.md files stay
# tracked as scaffold: prompts cite the templates by path, so a fresh clone
# must hold them.
#
# To keep other work/ paths in git, re-include them after the block, e.g.
#   !work/worker-logs/
#   !work/done/
# Files already tracked under work/ stay tracked until you run the
# `git rm --cached` command that `specy-road upgrade` prints.
#
# Derived indexes for `specy-road history` and `specy-road search`
# (.specyrd/cache/). Rebuilt from git and the working tree on demand, so they
# are never committed; .specyrd/manifest.json, when present, stays tracked.
#
# roadmap.md and roadmap-context.md are deliberately absent from this file.
# Both are generated, and both are COMMITTED: `roadmap.md` is the human index
# and `roadmap-context.md` (specy-road digest) is what an agent reads instead of
# crawling planning/ and work/. Regenerate them when the graph changes; gate CI
# on `specy-road export --check` and `specy-road digest --check`.
#
# Per-checkout capacity pauses (available / paused_until) without pushing the
# shared roster; merged at runtime with roadmap/orchestration.yaml. The ignore
# rule lives in agent_ignores.GITIGNORE_LINES (managed block below).
